---
/*
  THE INSTAGRAM GLYPH, drawn to their rules and to ours (2026-08-10).

  WHY IT EXISTS. Every other tile on this site leads to a piece. The four
  squares in the strip lead OFF the site, to a post, and nothing said so: a
  reader tapping one had no way to know the site was about to hand them to
  another app. The square shape alone is the recognition signal for what the
  strip IS (section 71); the glyph is the signal for what a tap DOES.

  THEIR RULES, and how each is met:

  - The glyph is not redrawn, restretched, rotated, or given effects. It sits on
    a locked square viewBox with `aspect-ratio: 1`, so no parent can squash it.
  - A SOLID one-colour glyph is the sanctioned substitute where the full-colour
    gradient cannot be used, and this site has exactly two colours (standing
    rule 11: text over a photograph is solid paper or solid ink, never a scrim
    and never a gray). It takes `currentColor`, which is the frame's own measured
    caption polarity, so it obeys their rule and ours at once.
  - It is never locked up with the site's own monogram, which would read as a
    partnership. It appears on the squares and beside the handle, nowhere else.
  - Clear space is held around it by padding rather than by hope.

  OURS, and marked as ours: the rendered size and the amount of clear space.
  `--ig-mark` has a floor in px, so the glyph cannot be scaled down into an
  illegible smudge by a future container.

  Decorative by default: on a square, the link already carries a label naming
  Instagram, and a second announcement would be noise. `title` turns it into a
  labelled image for the cases where it stands alone.
*/
interface Props {
  /** An accessible name. Omitted, the glyph is decorative. */
  title?: string | null;
  class?: string;
}

const {title = null, class: className = ""} = Astro.props;
---

<svg
  class:list={["ig-mark", className]}
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="2"
  role={title ? "img" : "presentation"}
  aria-hidden={title ? undefined : "true"}
>
  {title && <title>{title}</title>}
  {/* the rounded square, the lens, and the dot: the three parts, unaltered */}
  <rect x="2" y="2" width="20" height="20" rx="5.5" />
  <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4.75" />
  <circle cx="17.6" cy="6.4" r="1.4" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
</svg>
